{
  "raw": {
    "https://www.lindsey.edu/about-lwc/Offices-and-Services/Human-Resources/job-opportunities.cfm#assistant-athletic-trainer": {
      "title": "ASSISTANT ATHLETIC TRAINER",
      "description": "ASSISTANT ATHLETIC TRAINER. Posted: 9/17/2026 Lindsey Wilson University is searching for an Assistant Athletic Trainer. Lindsey Wilson University is a member of the Mid-South Conference and the National Association for Intercollegiate Athletics (NAIA) and sponsors 28 varsity/club sports programs consisting of 36 teams and 800+ student-athletes. The position offers the opportunity to work with highly competitive NAIA athletic programs. Requirements include bachelor’s or master’s degree in athletic training from a CAATE accredited University. Must be Board of Certification (BOCATC) certified; Must be licensed or eligible for licensure through the Kentucky Medical Board of Licensure; Must be certified in ALS/BLS from the American Heart Association/American Red Cross. Must have a valid driver’s license and have a current NPI Number. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Applied Knowledge: Assistant athletic trainers must have knowledge of a large range of medical problems and conditions, including but not limited to: Orthopedic/Musculoskeletal, General Medical, Psychological, etc. Assessment and evaluation skills need to be proficient, with areas of growth to occur. Decision Making Skills: Assistant athletic trainers need to have the ability to think critically regarding assessment, treatment, rehabilitation, and return to play decisions, as per standing orders and state licensure guidelines. Attention to Detail: Assistant athletic trainers should be thorough and detailed in their injury documentation and tracking, along with their assessment and evaluation of athletic-related injuries and illnesses. Interpersonal Skills: Assistant athletic trainers must have the ability to communicate effectively in high stress/pressure situations when talking to student-athletes, medical professionals, staff and coaches. Organization: Assistant athletic trainers must have the ability to organize, prioritize, and perform multiple tasks with little to no supervision. Autonomy: Assistant athletic trainers need to be able to make independent decisions regarding assessments, treatments, rehabilitation and return to play. Assistant athletic trainers need to be able to work independently, with the cumulative support of the Sports Medicine department. Specific Duties and Responsibilities: Onsite care and management of injuries and illnesses including prevention, evaluation, management, and rehabilitation. Assess risk of injury, perform ergonomic evaluation and coaching, self-care implementation and overall wellness promotion. Coordinate and implement injury prevention programs and customized preventative strategies and program for each patient. Minimize risk of injury through awareness, education and prevention strategies. Provide accommodation recommendations, related to sport, for student-athletes with restrictions and/or limitation based upon clinician evaluation and assessments. Communicate with physicians and coaching staff regarding injury status of student-athletes. Responsible for administrative duties including electronic documentation for all patient encounters, filing and management of insurance claims and follow-ups, management and coordination of doctors/surgery appointments. Description of Athletics Program/Assignments: Lindsey Wilson University is a member of the Mid-South Conference and the National Association for Intercollegiate Athletics (NAIA) and sponsors 27 varsity/club sports programs consisting of 36 teams and 800+ student-athletes. Sporting assignments will be decided upon successful hiring and personal preferences. Sporting assignments could include: Football (2), Men’s and Women’s Soccer, XC and Track/Field, Men’s and Women’s Basketball, Cheerleading/Dance, Men’s and Women’s Swim, Softball, Men’s and Women’s Golf, Men’s and Women’s Bowling. Travel Responsibilities: Some travel may be required, based upon game coverage and athletic training room needs. Overnight travel may occur with conference games, and post-season/nationals travel as well. Physical Requirements: Lifting and carrying heavy objects. Medium strength is required to position student-athletes for examination. May assist student-athletes as needed, helping them on and off the exam table, or assisting athletes off the field for further evaluation. Ability to work a flexible schedule, including evenings, weekends and holidays. Supervisory Responsibilities: Assistant athletic trainers will help supervise MSAT students and athletic training observation students, both within the athletic training room and at the sport practice/game sites. To apply, please submit a letter of interest and resume, and three references through the Lindsey Wilson University online employment application . The selection process will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Lindsey Wilson University is an EOE."
    },
    "https://www.lindsey.edu/about-lwc/Offices-and-Services/Human-Resources/job-opportunities.cfm#enrollment-coordinator-western-kentucky-service-region": {
      "title": "ENROLLMENT COORDINATOR- WESTERN KENTUCKY SERVICE REGION",
      "description": "ENROLLMENT COORDINATOR- WESTERN KENTUCKY SERVICE REGION. Posted: 9/17/2026 Lindsey Wilson University is seeking an Enrollment Coordinator to serve the western Kentucky service region. This position focuses on building relationships across the region, connecting with local schools, community organizations, and employers, to help students access educational opportunities. The coordinator will recruit for all LWU programs and guide students through the admissions process from first contact to enrollment. Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree required Strong communication and relationship-building skills Experience in recruitment, marketing, or community engagement preferred Valid driver’s license and ability to travel locally The ideal candidate is community-minded, dependable, and passionate about helping students succeed. This role is perfect for someone who values relationships and wants to make a meaningful impact in the region. To apply, please submit a letter of interest and resume, and three references through the Lindsey Wilson University online employment application . The selection process will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Lindsey Wilson University is an EOE."
    },
    "https://www.lindsey.edu/about-lwc/Offices-and-Services/Human-Resources/job-opportunities.cfm#carpenter": {
      "title": "CARPENTER",
      "description": "CARPENTER. Posted: 9/04/2026 Lindsey Wilson University is seeking an energetic individual to assume carpenter duties. Selected applicants must enjoy working with young adults, faculty and staff in a living/learning environment. The Carpenter will be responsible for a wide range of carpentry tasks including installation, repair, and maintenance of various structures and fixtures across campus. This position plays a crucial role in ensuring the safety, functionality, and aesthetic appeal of our facilities. High school diploma or equivalent required. Vocational or technical training in carpentry is preferred. To apply, please submit a letter of interest and resume through the Lindsey Wilson University online employment application . The selection process will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Lindsey Wilson University is an EOE."
    },
    "https://www.lindsey.edu/about-lwc/Offices-and-Services/Human-Resources/job-opportunities.cfm#apprentice-carpenter": {
      "title": "APPRENTICE CARPENTER",
      "description": "APPRENTICE CARPENTER. Posted: 9/04/2026 Lindsey Wilson University is seeking an energetic individual to assume Apprentice Carpenter duties. Selected applicants must enjoy working with young adults, faculty and staff in a living/learning environment. The Carpenter will be responsible for a wide range of carpentry tasks including installation, repair, and maintenance of various structures and fixtures across campus. This position plays a crucial role in ensuring the safety, functionality, and aesthetic appeal of our facilities. High school diploma or equivalent required. Vocational or technical training in carpentry is preferred. To apply, please submit a letter of interest and resume through the Lindsey Wilson University online employment application . The selection process will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Lindsey Wilson University is an EOE."
    },
    "https://www.lindsey.edu/about-lwc/Offices-and-Services/Human-Resources/job-opportunities.cfm#wordpress-developer-intern": {
      "title": "WORDPRESS DEVELOPER INTERN",
      "description": "WORDPRESS DEVELOPER INTERN. Posted: 5/26/2026 Lindsey Wilson University is seeking a motivated and creative WordPress Developer Intern to assist with the migration and redevelopment of the existing www.lindsey.edu website into WordPress. This internship position reports to the IT Department and works closely with the Public Relations to support website content, communications, and digital initiatives. This is an excellent opportunity for someone looking to gain hands-on experience working on a live educational website conversion project while building their portfolio and professional skills. Assist with converting the existing Lindsey.edu website to WordPress Develop, maintain, and improve WordPress pages, themes, and functionality Customize WordPress themes, plugins, and page layouts Collaborate regularly with the Public Relations Department during normal business hours to support website updates, branding, campaigns, and communications Integrate and work with third-party APIs and external data sources as needed Ensure website pages are visually appealing, responsive, and user-friendly Identify and troubleshoot website issues as needed Independently manage assigned tasks and meet project deadlines Support the IT Department in maintaining website functionality and performance Requirements Proficiency with WordPress website development and management Strong understanding of web design principles and user experience Good grasp of consuming and integrating APIs Working knowledge of HTML, CSS, JavaScript, and related web technologies Ability to meet and collaborate with Public Relations staff during standard business hours Self-motivated and capable of working independently Strong communication and organizational skills Portfolio or examples of previous WordPress/design work preferred What You'll Gain Real-world experience contributing to a large-scale website conversion project Opportunity to build and strengthen WordPress development, API integration, and design skills Experience working with both IT and Public Relations professionals Portfolio-building opportunities and professional references upon successful completion This is a non-paying internship position intended for individuals seeking practical experience in WordPress development, website design, API integration, and digital communications. To apply, please submit your resume along with any relevant portfolio links or examples of previous work through the Lindsey Wilson University online employment application . Lindsey Wilson University is an EOE."
    },
    "https://www.lindsey.edu/about-lwc/Offices-and-Services/Human-Resources/job-opportunities.cfm#flag-football-graduate-assistant": {
      "title": "FLAG FOOTBALL GRADUATE ASSISTANT",
      "description": "FLAG FOOTBALL GRADUATE ASSISTANT. Posted: 5/7/2026 Lindsey Wilson University, located in Columbia, Kentucky, is seeking applicants for a Flag Football Graduate Assistant. Lindsey Wilson, a member of the Mid-South Conference and the NAIA, sponsors twenty-eight varsity athletic programs and has 800+ student-athletes participating in total. GA duties include, but are not limited to the following: conducting practices, weight training sessions, conditioning sessions, recruiting, monitoring academic progress of the student-athletes, fundraising, scheduling, and other coaching/administrative duties under direction of the head coach. Review of applications will begin immediately. A bachelor’s degree and valid driver’s license is required; previous collegiate playing and/or coaching experience preferred. The selected candidate will be provided a $5,000 stipend, graduate tuition at LWU (18 hours/year), on-campus housing and meals for their service. To apply, submit a cover letter, recommendations and resume through the Lindsey Wilson University online employment application . The selection process will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Lindsey Wilson University is an EOE."
    },
    "https://www.lindsey.edu/about-lwc/Offices-and-Services/Human-Resources/job-opportunities.cfm#enrollment-coordinator-for-educational-outreach-louisville-campus": {
      "title": "ENROLLMENT COORDINATOR FOR EDUCATIONAL OUTREACH - LOUISVILLE CAMPUS",
      "description": "ENROLLMENT COORDINATOR FOR EDUCATIONAL OUTREACH - LOUISVILLE CAMPUS. Posted: 1/16/2026 Lindsey Wilson University is seeking applicants for an Enrollment Coordinator for our Louisville campus in Kentucky. This position is located on-site at our Louisville, KY campus. The coordinator is responsible for recruitment in Louisville/Lexington, Kentucky and surrounding areas throughout the region. Primary responsibilities include but are not limited to recruiting for all LWU programs, mentoring students throughout the admissions process, and functioning as a contact between the University, local agencies, and related educational institutions. Qualifications include: A bachelor’s degree, experience in marketing, networking, communication skills, and a valid driver’s license. The coordinator will demonstrate understanding of LWU’s philosophy of actively caring for students and providing excellent customer service to potential and enrolled students. Successful applicant must be reliable, trustworthy and able to successfully pass a background check. To apply, please submit a letter of interest, resume, and three references through the Lindsey Wilson University online employment application . The selection process will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. LWU is an equal opportunity employer committed to assembling a caring, equity-focused faculty committed to supporting “every student, every day.” LWU strives to hire qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, national origin, age, disability, genetic information or status as a protected veteran."
    },
    "https://www.lindsey.edu/about-lwc/Offices-and-Services/Human-Resources/job-opportunities.cfm#adjunct-faculty-epidemiology": {
      "title": "ADJUNCT FACULTY – EPIDEMIOLOGY",
      "description": "ADJUNCT FACULTY – EPIDEMIOLOGY. Posted: 6/16/2025 Lindsey Wilson University is seeking a dynamic and experienced professional to join our Education Program as an Adjunct Instructor to teach Health Education courses online. The successful candidate will bring both academic and practical expertise to educate and inspire the next generation of public health professionals. Job responsibilities include teaching undergraduate courses in Health Education, specifically, beginning with the EDUC Epidemiology course in fall of 2025, develop syllabi, lesson plans, and assessments in alignment with course objectives, engage students through interactive online lectures, discussions, and applied assignments, provide timely feedback and support to students, utilize the institution’s learning management system (LMS) Canvas for communication and grading and maintain availability for student questions and academic support A Master’s degree in Epidemiology, Public Health, or a related field is required, and a terminal degree is preferred. Prior online or hybrid teaching experience at the college/university level is strongly preferred along with demonstrated expertise in health, epidemiological methods and data analysis. The position requires strong communication and organizational skills. Review of applications will begin immediately. To apply, please submit a letter of interest, curriculum vitae including names and contact information for three professional references, statement of teaching philosophy, unofficial copies of all graduate transcripts (official copies must be submitted prior to hiring) through the Lindsey Wilson University online employment application . Review of applicants will begin immediately and be ongoing until the position is filled. LWU is an equal opportunity employer committed to assembling a caring, equity focused faculty committed to supporting “every student, every day”. LWU strives to hire qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, national origin, age, disability, genetic information or status as a protected veteran."
    },
    "https://www.lindsey.edu/about-lwc/Offices-and-Services/Human-Resources/job-opportunities.cfm#part-time-dining-center-seasonal-worker": {
      "title": "PART-TIME DINING CENTER SEASONAL WORKER",
      "description": "PART-TIME DINING CENTER SEASONAL WORKER. Posted: 09/05/2023 Lindsey Wilson University is seeking applicants for the position of a generalized part time seasonal worker. A successful applicant must be highly organized and a self-starter. Responsibilities include general prepping, sanitation, dish washing and helping in other areas when needed. Send letter of interest and resume to: Human Resources, Lindsey Wilson University, 210 Lindsey Wilson Street, Columbia, Kentucky 42728, fax 270-384-7373 or e-mail hr@lindsey.edu or apply on-line at www.lindsey.edu. LWU is an EOE employer."
    },
    "https://www.lindsey.edu/about-lwc/Offices-and-Services/Human-Resources/job-opportunities.cfm#student-support-specialist": {
      "title": "STUDENT SUPPORT SPECIALIST",
      "description": "STUDENT SUPPORT SPECIALIST. Posted: 10/26/2026 Lindsey Wilson University is seeking applicants for a Student Support Specialist to join our Registrar's Office team. The Registrar's Office is responsible for the collection, management, and housing of all official student records. The Student Support Specialist duties will include, but are not limited to, customer service, student registration, file management and correspondence. Applicants must have excellent time management and organizational skills. Computer skills must include proficiency in Windows and Microsoft Office software, excellent communication skills and the willingness and capability of learning various specialized software utilized by the University. We are looking for an individual who has a strong sense of integrity who can maintain strict confidentiality who possesses a desire to serve our campus community through active caring and meaningful support. A Bachelor's Degree or a minimum of 2 years of office experience is required. Those with prior experience in Higher Education Administration are preferred. To apply, please submit a letter of interest and resume through the Lindsey Wilson University online employment application . The selection process will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Lindsey Wilson University is an EOE."
    },
    "https://www.lindsey.edu/about-lwc/Offices-and-Services/Human-Resources/job-opportunities.cfm#assistant-professor-of-mathematics": {
      "title": "ASSISTANT PROFESSOR OF MATHEMATICS",
      "description": "ASSISTANT PROFESSOR OF MATHEMATICS. Posted: 10/21/2026 Lindsey Wilson University (LWU), a United Methodist affiliated liberal arts college located in south central Kentucky, invites applications for a full-time faculty position in Mathematics to begin in January or August 2027. The preferred candidate will hold a Ph.D. in mathematics but master’s degree candidates will be considered. The successful candidate will teach courses in the general education mathematics curriculum, along with various courses across the mathematics major curriculum. This position emphasizes teaching, advising, scholarship (broadly defined), and service to the university. Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. To apply, please submit a letter of interest, curriculum vitae including names and contact information for three professional references, statement of teaching philosophy, statement of research philosophy, and unofficial copies of all graduate transcripts (official copies must be submitted prior to hiring) through the Lindsey Wilson University online employment application . Review of applicants will begin immediately and be ongoing until the position is filled. LWU is an equal opportunity employer committed to assembling a caring, equity-focused faculty committed to supporting “every student, every day.” LWC strives to hire qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, national origin, age, disability, genetic information or status as a protected veteran."
    },
    "https://www.lindsey.edu/about-lwc/Offices-and-Services/Human-Resources/job-opportunities.cfm#assistant-professor-of-biology-molecular-cell-biology": {
      "title": "ASSISTANT PROFESSOR OF BIOLOGY- MOLECULAR/CELL BIOLOGY",
      "description": "ASSISTANT PROFESSOR OF BIOLOGY- MOLECULAR/CELL BIOLOGY. Posted: 10/21/2026 Lindsey Wilson University, a United Methodist affiliated liberal arts college located in south central Kentucky, is seeking applicants for a full-time faculty position in Biology with expertise in molecular biology, cell biology, genetics, biochemistry, or a closely related field. Job responsibilities include teaching undergraduate courses in molecular biology, genetics, cell biology, biochemistry, and related areas, develop syllabi and assessments in alignment with course objectives, engage students through effective classroom instruction and active learning, provide timely feedback and academic support to students, mentor and advise undergraduate students, maintain appropriate availability for student questions and academic support, engage in scholarly activity appropriate to the discipline, and collaborate effectively with faculty and colleagues. A Ph.D. in Molecular Biology, Cell Biology, Genetics, Biochemistry, Biology, or a closely related field is required. Demonstrated expertise in molecular biology through research, publications, and/or professional experience is strongly preferred. A record of effective teaching at the undergraduate and/or graduate level is preferred. The position requires strong written and oral communication skills, as well as demonstrated ability to mentor and advise students and collaborate effectively with colleagues. The successful candidate will contribute to the undergraduate Biology curriculum through teaching, student mentoring and advising, scholarship, and collaboration with colleagues. To apply, please submit a letter of interest, curriculum vitae including names and contact information for three professional references, statement of teaching philosophy, statement of research philosophy, and unofficial copies of all graduate transcripts (official copies must be submitted prior to hiring) through the Lindsey Wilson University online employment application . Review of applicants will begin immediately and be ongoing until the position is filled. LWU is an equal opportunity employer committed to assembling a caring, equity-focused faculty committed to supporting “every student, every day.” LWC strives to hire qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, national origin, age, disability, genetic information or status as a protected veteran."
    },
    "https://www.lindsey.edu/about-lwc/Offices-and-Services/Human-Resources/job-opportunities.cfm#assistant-professor-of-communication": {
      "title": "ASSISTANT PROFESSOR OF COMMUNICATION",
      "description": "ASSISTANT PROFESSOR OF COMMUNICATION. Posted: 10/21/2026 Lindsey Wilson University, a United Methodist affiliated liberal arts college located in south central Kentucky, is seeking applicants for a full-time faculty position in Communication beginning in August 2027. interested candidates holding a Ph.D. in Communication or a closely related field with a minimum of 18 graduate semester hours of communication coursework are encouraged to apply; ABD will be considered. Candidates holding an M.A. in Communication with an exceptional history of teaching or professional experience may be considered at the rank of instructor. The successful candidate must demonstrate a commitment to teaching, academic advising, ongoing professional development, collaboration with other faculty, and service. To apply, please submit a letter of interest, curriculum vitae including names and contact information for three professional references, statement of teaching philosophy, unofficial copies of all graduate transcripts (official copies must be submitted prior to hiring), and the online employment application form through the Lindsey Wilson University online employment application. Review of applicants will begin immediately and be ongoing until the position is filled. All offers of employment are contingent upon the university’s verification of credentials and completing a criminal history check. For more information visit http://www.lindsey.edu . LWU is an equal opportunity employer committed to assembling a caring, equity-focused faculty committed to supporting “every student, every day.” LWC strives to hire qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, national origin, age, disability, genetic information or status as a protected veteran."
    },
    "https://www.lindsey.edu/about-lwc/Offices-and-Services/Human-Resources/job-opportunities.cfm#instructor-of-chemistry": {
      "title": "INSTRUCTOR OF CHEMISTRY",
      "description": "INSTRUCTOR OF CHEMISTRY. Posted: 10/21/2026 Lindsey Wilson University, a United Methodist affiliated liberal arts college located in south central Kentucky, is seeking applicants for a full-time faculty position in chemistry. The successful candidate will contribute to the undergraduate Nursing and General Education curricula through teaching, student mentoring and advising, scholarship, and collaboration with colleagues. Job responsibilities include teaching undergraduate courses in chemistry for pre-nursing majors, as well as topics in science courses for non-majors, develop syllabi and assessments in alignment with course objectives, engage students through effective classroom instruction and active learning, provide timely feedback and academic support to students, mentor and advise undergraduate students, maintain appropriate availability for student questions and academic support, engage in scholarship, and collaborate effectively with faculty and colleagues. A master’s degree in chemistry or a closely related field is required and a Ph.D. is preferred. Demonstrated expertise in chemistry through research, publications, and/or professional experience is strongly preferred. A record of effective teaching at the undergraduate and/or graduate level is preferred. The position requires strong written and oral communication skills, as well as demonstrated ability to mentor and advise students and collaborate effectively with colleagues. To apply, please submit a letter of interest, curriculum vitae including names and contact information for three professional references, statement of teaching philosophy, statement of research philosophy, and unofficial copies of all graduate transcripts (official copies must be submitted prior to hiring) through the Lindsey Wilson University online employment application . Review of applicants will begin immediately and be ongoing until the position is filled. LWU is an equal opportunity employer committed to assembling a caring, equity-focused faculty committed to supporting “every student, every day.” LWC strives to hire qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, national origin, age, disability, genetic information or status as a protected veteran."
    },
    "https://www.lindsey.edu/about-lwc/Offices-and-Services/Human-Resources/job-opportunities.cfm#payroll-associate": {
      "title": "PAYROLL ASSOCIATE",
      "description": "PAYROLL ASSOCIATE. Posted: 10/19/2026 Lindsey Wilson University is seeking applicants for a Payroll Associate to support the Payroll Clerk and Human Resources Office. This position will assist with all aspects of payroll processing, including data entry, tax payments, and reports. Additional responsibilities include processing employee benefits enrollment, maintaining personnel records, verifying employment documentation, and assisting with various Human Resources projects and events. The ideal candidate will demonstrate strong attention to detail, problem-solving abilities, and excellent organizational, interpersonal, and communication skills. Candidates should be able to maintain confidentiality, manage multiple priorities, adapt to changing demands, and consistently produce accurate and high-quality work. Bachelor’s degree in Accounting, Human Resources, or Business preferred . Proficiency in Microsoft Office applications, including Excel, Word, and PowerPoint is required. Experience with Banner Software is preferred. To apply, please submit a letter of interest and resume through the Lindsey Wilson University online employment application . The selection process will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Lindsey Wilson University is an EOE."
    }
  },
